@title Orchard Irrigation Schedule: Rule Check and Edit Sheet
@subtitle The current controller export, checked against the pump, water, power-price, dusk and crop rules
@width wide

! This page is a fixed check, not a live editor: it does not recalculate when you change a time. Edit the copy-out block at the bottom, then bring the changed zones back to be re-checked. The check below covers the schedule exactly as exported.

kpi Pump peak | 565 L/min | limit is 600 | good
kpi Days over water allocation | 5 of 7 | Mon, Tue, Wed, Fri, Sat | bad
kpi Water per week | 405,350 L | 364,000 L allowed | bad
kpi Dusk-buffer breaches | 1 | Z9 starts 19:00 | bad

# What the check found

table = rule,result,detail; Pump 600 L/min or less,Go,"The highest simultaneous load is 565 L/min on Wednesday (Z6 with Z7 or Z8, and Z5 with Z7). Z1 with Z2 would total 620 L/min, so their 15-minute gap (06:15 to 06:30) is what protects the pump."; Water 52,000 L per day,Failed,"Monday, Tuesday, Wednesday, Friday and Saturday are over. Only Thursday and Sunday are within the allocation."; No zone over 90 minutes,Go,"Z5 and Z6 run exactly 90 minutes, so they have no room to grow."; Nothing from 11:00 to 16:00,Go,"The latest morning finish is Z4 at 08:00 and the first evening start is Z9 at 19:00."; Nothing within an hour after dusk (18:40 to 19:40),Failed,"Z9 runs 19:00 to 19:30, inside the window."; Z7 never over 45 minutes,Go,"Z7 runs exactly 45 minutes."; Cherries dry for 3 days before picking (Bing from Oct 28),At risk,"Z7 is scheduled for Monday Oct 26, one of the three dry days, if Oct 28 is a Wednesday as it is in 2026. Rainier (Z8) has no picking date in the export, so it cannot be checked."; The four apple zones not watered on consecutive days,At risk,"The rule can be read two ways, and the schedule passes one and fails the other. See below."

# The schedule as exported

data schedule = zone,crop,start,run min,days,flow L/min,soil moisture %,notes; Z1,Honeycrisp apples,05:00,75,"Mon, Thu",310,24.5,"Young trees, planted 2023"
data schedule += Z2,Honeycrisp apples,06:30,75,"Mon, Thu",310,26.1,
data schedule += Z3,Fuji apples,05:30,60,"Tue, Fri",280,21.8,Drains fast; sandy patch near the road
data schedule += Z4,Fuji apples,07:00,60,"Tue, Fri",280,27.3,
data schedule += Z5,Bartlett pears,04:30,90,"Wed, Sat",345,30.2,“Wet corner” in NE rows; check for leaks
data schedule += Z6,Bartlett pears,06:15,90,"Wed, Sat",345,29.7,
data schedule += Z7,Cherries (Bing),05:45,45,"Mon, Wed, Fri",220,19.4,Needs deficit stress before harvest; do not exceed 45 min
data schedule += Z8,Cherries (Rainier),06:30,45,"Mon, Wed, Fri",220,,Sensor broken since Sept
data schedule += Z9,Nursery rows,19:00,30,Daily,95,33.8,Hand-watered Sundays
data schedule += Z10,Plum (Santa Rosa),21:30,80,"Tue, Sat",260,25.0,

table schedule

## The weekly pattern

A dot is a day the zone runs. Z9 is exported as Daily but its note says hand-watered Sundays, so its Sunday is a question mark.

table = zone,Mon,Tue,Wed,Thu,Fri,Sat,Sun; Z1,●,,,●,,,; Z2,●,,,●,,,; Z3,,●,,,●,,; Z4,,●,,,●,,; Z5,,,●,,,●,; Z6,,,●,,,●,; Z7,●,,●,,●,,; Z8,●,,●,,●,,; Z9,●,●,●,●,●,●,●?; Z10,,●,,,,●,

## What each zone draws

Litres per run is flow times run time. Weekly litres is litres per run times the days the zone runs.

table = zone,start,end,flow L/min,litres per run,runs per week,litres per week; Z1,05:00,06:15,310,"23,250",2,"46,500"; Z2,06:30,07:45,310,"23,250",2,"46,500"; Z3,05:30,06:30,280,"16,800",2,"33,600"; Z4,07:00,08:00,280,"16,800",2,"33,600"; Z5,04:30,06:00,345,"31,050",2,"62,100"; Z6,06:15,07:45,345,"31,050",2,"62,100"; Z7,05:45,06:30,220,"9,900",3,"29,700"; Z8,06:30,07:15,220,"9,900",3,"29,700"; Z9,19:00,19:30,95,"2,850",7,"19,950"; Z10,21:30,22:50,260,"20,800",2,"41,600"; **Total**,,,,,,**405,350**

# Pump limit: 600 L/min

The pump limit is a sum over whatever is running at the same moment. These pairs add up to more than 600 L/min and must never overlap:

- Any two of Z1, Z2, Z5 and Z6 (310 + 310 = 620 at the lowest, up to 345 + 345 = 690).
- Z5 or Z6 with Z3 or Z4 (345 + 280 = 625).
- Z5 or Z6 with Z10 (345 + 260 = 605).
- Z7 and Z8 together with any zone except Z9 (440 + 160 or more).

These pairs are fine: Z1 or Z2 with Z3 or Z4 (590, only 10 L/min of headroom), Z3 with Z4 (560), and Z7 or Z8 with any single other zone (at most 565).

The schedule only overlaps zones in these places, all within the limit:

table = day,zones,overlap,load L/min; Mon,Z1 with Z7,05:45 to 06:15,530; Mon,Z2 with Z8,06:30 to 07:15,530; Wed,Z5 with Z7,05:45 to 06:00,565; Wed,Z6 with Z7,06:15 to 06:30,565; Wed,Z6 with Z8,06:30 to 07:15,565; Fri,Z3 with Z7,05:45 to 06:30,500; Fri,Z4 with Z8,07:00 to 07:15,500

Wednesday is the tightest day: four zones in the morning and the nursery in the evening.

data wed = zone,start,end; Z5 pears,4.5,6.0; Z6 pears,6.25,7.75; Z7 Bing cherries,5.75,6.5; Z8 Rainier cherries,6.5,7.25; Z9 nursery,19.0,19.5

chart range wed from=start to=end target="18.67 dusk" title="Wednesday, hours on the 24-hour clock (6.25 is 06:15, 19.5 is 19:30)"

# Water allocation: 52,000 L per day

This is where the schedule breaks. Daily totals are the litres from each zone that runs that day.

data water = day,litres; Mon,69150; Tue,57250; Wed,84750; Thu,49350; Fri,56250; Sat,85750; Sun,2850

chart bar water y=litres target="52000 allocation" unit=L labels title="Litres per day against the 52,000 L allocation"

table = day,zones running,litres,against 52000 L,verdict; Mon,"Z1, Z2, Z7, Z8, Z9","69,150","17,150 over",Failed; Tue,"Z3, Z4, Z9, Z10","57,250","5,250 over",Failed; Wed,"Z5, Z6, Z7, Z8, Z9","84,750","32,750 over",Failed; Thu,"Z1, Z2, Z9","49,350","2,650 spare",Go; Fri,"Z3, Z4, Z7, Z8, Z9","56,250","4,250 over",Failed; Sat,"Z5, Z6, Z9, Z10","85,750","33,750 over",Failed; Sun,"Z9 only, if the controller runs it","2,850","49,150 spare",Go

!! Moving start times cannot fix this. Even if the same water were spread perfectly over seven days, the week would need 405,350 L against 364,000 L allowed (52,000 x 7), about 41,350 L too much. Spare daily capacity exists only on Sunday and, slightly, on Thursday. Run times, days or the allocation figure itself have to change, and that is your decision.

This check uses flow times run time for each zone and assumes the flow figures in the export are what each zone really draws. If the 52,000 L allocation is measured differently (for example weekly, or at the meter), the verdict changes.

# Dusk buffer: nothing between 18:40 and 19:40

Dusk is about 18:40 this month and moves through the year, so the window moves with it. Z9 (nursery) starts at 19:00 and runs to 19:30, inside the window. Z10 at 21:30 is clear.

# Cherries before picking

Bing picking starts Oct 28, so Z7 must not be watered on the 3 days before: Oct 25, 26 and 27. In 2026 those are Sunday, Monday and Tuesday, and Z7 runs Monday, Wednesday and Friday, so **Monday Oct 26 has to be skipped**. A weekly schedule cannot skip one date by itself; that needs a one-off override or a manual change.

The export has no picking date for Rainier cherries (Z8), so the check cannot say whether Z8 has a dry period coming. Z8 also has no soil moisture reading (sensor broken since Sept).

# Apple zones on consecutive days

The four apple zones (Z1 to Z4) are watered on Monday, Tuesday, Thursday and Friday. The rule "should not all be watered on consecutive days" can mean two things:

- **No back-to-back apple days at all.** Fails: Monday is followed by Tuesday, and Thursday by Friday.
- **No long unbroken run of apple days.** Passes: the longest run is two days, with Wednesday, Saturday and Sunday off.

Tell me which one you meant and the check can be settled.

# Questions the export cannot answer

- Z9 is exported as Daily, but the note says hand-watered Sundays. Should the controller run it on Sunday?
- Is the 52,000 L figure a hard daily cap, and is it measured the way flow times run time is?
- When does Rainier (Z8) picking start?
- Z8 has no moisture reading, and Z5 has the wettest reading (30.2%) with the longest runs and a note to check for leaks. Neither can be judged from the numbers given.
- Peak power ($0.31/kWh) versus off-peak ($0.11/kWh): nothing runs in the 11:00 to 16:00 window, so there is no peak cost to count, and the export has no pump kWh to price the rest.

# Proposals (not yet accepted)

These are proposals, not values you gave me.

1. **Proposal: Z9 start at 19:40** (ends 20:10) to clear the dusk window. Any start from 19:40 on works, or any start by 18:10 so it finishes by 18:40. The window will shift as dusk changes.
2. **Proposal: skip Z7 on Monday Oct 26** with a one-off override, for the Bing dry period.
3. **Decision needed: water allocation.** I have not proposed new run times, because the right cuts depend on which crops you can afford to shorten.

